From 852110d9269bcc63104bc069bde5a494f2046107 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:37:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08082/11362] [outer-loop] Enable the layer split in the
 outer-loop harnesses (11 sites)

Operator choice: enable for the outer loop only, while the conductor is down
(stopped since 2026-07-27). The conductor's systemd drop-in is untouched, so the
standing 2026-06-27 allocation is not contravened.

"1,0", NOT "0,1". The SPLIT is identical either way, but the DEGRADE order is
not, and the fallback scans the list in order. Verified live:

  both cards free            -> split across [1, 0]      38.83 tok/s
  gpu0 busy (conductor back) -> pins gpu1  = its OWN card, allocation respected
  gpu1 busy                  -> pins gpu0  = borrows, only as a fallback

With "0,1" the middle case would have tried to take the conductor's card first.
Left as setdefault, so an explicit export still wins.

SCOPE -- what was deliberately NOT changed:

- `python/carnot/experiment_NNNN_*.py` (12 sites). These are COMPLETED
  experiments; their env pin documents the configuration a past run used.
  Editing them would rewrite the record of how those results were produced.
- `scripts/arc_llm_on_contention_probe.py`. It launches K concurrent servers on
  ONE card on purpose -- that pin IS the independent variable. Splitting would
  change what the probe measures.
- `scripts/experiments/exp_phase_d_musr_trace_regen.py`, same reasoning as the
  completed experiments.

A FALSE PROVENANCE FIELD THIS CHANGE WOULD OTHERWISE HAVE CREATED. Four
harnesses hardcoded `"gpu": 1` into their artifact's model_specs. Under a split
that literal becomes a false declaration of where the model ran. Replaced with
the actual env value in arc_end_to_end_goal_gate.py,
arc_end_to_end_goal_gate_reauthored.py, arc_oracle_perception_goal_ablation.py
and arc_structured_nav_scored_ab.py. (arc_holdout_generalization_probe.py's
`cuda_gpu1_pinned` correctly evaluates to False under a split, and
arc_scored_path_lever_harness.py's `gpu_pin=` reports the raw value -- both
already honest, left alone.)

Freshness cascade: 4 artifacts REBUILT (early_stop_grace_sweep,
max_actions_answer, reset_charge_attribution, scored_path_lever_ab). Every one
moved ZERO measurement values -- the only changes are provenance.code[N].bytes,
the recorded source sizes of the files I edited. That is the expected signature
of an inert dependency change. The fifth (llm_on_wallclock_envelope) has no
rebuild_command -- a live multi-hour GPU measurement, where re-running produces
a NEW measurement rather than a reproduction -- so it got an APPENDED
acknowledgement citing those four rebuilds as its evidence.

DIFF NOISE, DISCLOSED: four of the eleven scripts carried pre-existing
formatting debt, so `ruff format` rewrapped unrelated lines in them.
Unavoidable -- the pre-commit hook reformats anything staged. A first pass also
reformatted 31 files I had NOT touched; those were reverted before staging
(`git status` before `git add`, per the Test-Run Record Integrity rule).

